<http://data.silknow.org/object/3c03c494-40cd-3014-afb0-ca58a2372704/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Pair of black silk shoes for Han men. The uppers are of black silk and are lined with white cotton, with leather (or rubber according to Wrigglesworth) piping at the front and back seams to reinforce the shape. Their 1.8 cm-think soles may have been made of layers of felted paper with layers of leather stitched together at the bottom, and whitened around the edges."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3c03c494-40cd-3014-afb0-ca58a2372704> .

